{
 "Actor, Judge, or Teacher? · REAL Lab Blog": "Actor, Judge, or Teacher? · REAL Lab 博客",
 "Decision models such as JEV struggle to act on tasks whose subgoals must be met in order, yet judged in hindsight they teach a 1.5B policy that outperforms them: 72.8% → 82.9% on ALFWorld and 56.8% → 71.4% on WebShop.": "JEV 这类决策模型自己执行时，常在子目标有先后顺序的任务上出错；但让它在回合结束后回头打分，教出的 1.5B 策略反而比它强。与只用 GRPO 相比，ALFWorld 成功率从 72.8% 提升到 82.9%，WebShop 从 56.8% 提升到 71.4%。",
 "A decision model that acts poorly can still teach well, if it is asked whether each action helped and shown the whole trajectory.": "决策模型自己动手常出错，却能当好老师。前提是问对问题：问每个动作有没有帮上忙，并且让它看完整条轨迹。",
 "<a href=\"../../blog.html\">Blog</a><span class=\"dot\"></span><span>November 22, 2026</span><span class=\"dot\"></span><span>Agentic AI · Reinforcement learning</span><span class=\"dot\"></span><span>14 min read</span>": "<a href=\"../../blog.html\">博客</a><span class=\"dot\"></span><span>2026 年 11 月 22 日</span><span class=\"dot\"></span><span>智能体 · 强化学习</span><span class=\"dot\"></span><span>阅读约 14 分钟</span>",
 "Decision models answer a question with a choice and a probability, so the same model can pick an agent's actions, grade them, or teach a policy. We find that a model which acts poorly can still teach well, as long as it is asked the right question and shown the whole trajectory.": "决策模型回答问题时，给出一个选项和每个选项的概率。所以同一个模型有三种用法：替智能体选动作，当执行者（Actor）；给动作打分，当裁判（Judge）；指导策略训练，当老师（Teacher）。我们发现，自己动手常出错的模型也能当好老师，前提是问对问题，并让它看到完整轨迹。",
 "<sup>1</sup>Zhejiang University <sup>2</sup>Baidu Inc. · *Equal contribution †Corresponding author": "<sup>1</sup>浙江大学 <sup>2</sup>百度 · *同等贡献 †通讯作者",
 "<a href=\"#roles\"><span class=\"n\">1</span>Three ways to ask</a>": "<a href=\"#roles\"><span class=\"n\">1</span>同一个模型，三种问法</a>",
 "<a href=\"#actor\"><span class=\"n\">2</span>As an actor</a>": "<a href=\"#actor\"><span class=\"n\">2</span>当执行者</a>",
 "<a href=\"#actor-order\">Ordered subgoals</a>": "<a href=\"#actor-order\">子目标有先后</a>",
 "<a href=\"#actor-distract\">Distraction, not ignorance</a>": "<a href=\"#actor-distract\">不是不会，是分心</a>",
 "<a href=\"#judge\"><span class=\"n\">3</span>As a judge</a>": "<a href=\"#judge\"><span class=\"n\">3</span>当裁判</a>",
 "<a href=\"#judge-question\">Ask about the action</a>": "<a href=\"#judge-question\">问动作，不问结局</a>",
 "<a href=\"#judge-context\">Show the whole trajectory</a>": "<a href=\"#judge-context\">看完整条轨迹</a>",
 "<a href=\"#teacher\"><span class=\"n\">4</span>As a teacher</a>": "<a href=\"#teacher\"><span class=\"n\">4</span>当老师</a>",
 "<a href=\"#teacher-signal\">From scores to advantages</a>": "<a href=\"#teacher-signal\">从打分到优势</a>",
 "<a href=\"#teacher-results\">Results</a>": "<a href=\"#teacher-results\">实验结果</a>",
 "<a href=\"#teacher-surpass\">Learning beyond the teacher</a>": "<a href=\"#teacher-surpass\">学生超过老师</a>",
 "<a href=\"#takeaways\"><span class=\"n\">5</span>Takeaways</a>": "<a href=\"#takeaways\"><span class=\"n\">5</span>几点启示</a>",
 "<a href=\"#roles\">Three ways to ask a decision model</a>": "<a href=\"#roles\">同一个模型，三种问法</a>",
 "<a href=\"#actor\">As an actor</a>": "<a href=\"#actor\">当执行者</a>",
 "<a href=\"#judge\">As a judge</a>": "<a href=\"#judge\">当裁判</a>",
 "<a href=\"#teacher\">As a teacher</a>": "<a href=\"#teacher\">当老师</a>",
 "<a href=\"#takeaways\">Takeaways</a>": "<a href=\"#takeaways\">几点启示</a>",
 "A <em>decision model</em> answers a question about a context with a typed output, such as a choice among options with a probability for each, instead of free text. Because any question can be asked about any state, one model can choose an agent's next action, evaluate an action already taken, or score every action of a policy during reinforcement learning. So far these models have mostly been judged by how well they act.": "<em>决策模型</em>不输出自由文本。它针对给定的上下文回答问题，答案有固定格式，比如从几个选项里选一个，同时给出每个选项的概率。问题和状态可以任意搭配，所以同一个模型既能为智能体选下一步动作，也能评估已经做过的动作，还能在强化学习中给策略的每个动作打分。不过到目前为止，大家评价这类模型，主要看它自己执行得怎么样。",
 "We asked whether a model that acts poorly can still teach well. On ALFWorld, JEV completes <strong>42.9%</strong> of tasks when it chooses the actions itself. Used instead to score each action of a 1.5B policy during GRPO training, it raises that policy's success over GRPO alone from 72.8% to <strong>82.9%</strong> on the same tasks, and from 56.8% to <strong>71.4%</strong> on WebShop. <strong>The difference comes from timing: an actor must anticipate consequences, whereas a judge that reads the finished episode can see them.</strong>": "我们想弄清楚：自己执行得差的模型，能不能教得好？在 ALFWorld 上，JEV 亲自选动作，只能完成 <strong>42.9%</strong> 的任务。换一种用法，让它在 GRPO 训练中给 1.5B 策略的每个动作打分，策略在同一批任务上的成功率就从单用 GRPO 的 72.8% 提高到 <strong>82.9%</strong>；在 WebShop 上，则从 56.8% 提高到 <strong>71.4%</strong>。<strong>差别出在时机：执行者只能事先预判后果，裁判读的是已经结束的回合，后果就摆在眼前。</strong>",
 "The benefit is not automatic. It appears only when the model is asked whether each action <em>helped achieve the goal</em>, rather than whether the task will succeed, and only when it sees the <em>whole trajectory</em> rather than the steps leading up to the action. Queried this way after each episode, a frozen decision model provides step-level supervision for 22 to 30 USD of API calls per training run, with no step labels and no learned critic.": "这个收益有条件。问模型的，必须是每个动作<em>有没有帮助达成目标</em>，而不是任务会不会成功；给模型看的，必须是<em>完整轨迹</em>，而不只是这个动作之前的几步。照这样在每个回合结束后提问，参数冻结的决策模型就能提供步级监督：不需要步级标注，也不用训练 critic，每次训练的 API 花费只有 22 到 30 美元。",
 "<span class=\"n\">1</span>Three ways to ask a decision model": "<span class=\"n\">1</span>同一个模型，三种问法",
 "A decision model takes a <em>question</em> and a <em>context</em>. For a multiple-choice question it selects an option and assigns a probability to every option; for a yes/no question it returns one score in [0, 1]. We query the same model in three roles that differ only in what it is asked and how its answer is used.": "决策模型的输入有两部分：<em>问题</em>和<em>上下文</em>。遇到选择题，它选出一个选项，同时给每个选项一个概率；遇到是非题，它返回 [0, 1] 之间的一个分数。下面三种角色用的是同一个模型，区别只在问它什么、它的回答拿来做什么。",
 "<span class=\"role-a\">Actor.</span> At each step the model picks the next action from the valid commands, given the goal, the history and the current observation. The choice is executed.": "<span class=\"role-a\">执行者（Actor）。</span>每一步，模型根据目标、历史和当前观测，从合法命令里挑出下一步动作，然后执行。",
 "<span class=\"role-j\">Judge.</span> The model scores each action of a recorded trajectory. We vary what it sees, the trajectory up to the action (<em>Prefix</em>) or the whole trajectory (<em>Hindsight</em>), and what it is asked, whether the task will succeed after the action (<em>Value</em>) or whether the action helped achieve the goal (<em>Progress</em>).": "<span class=\"role-j\">裁判（Judge）。</span>模型给一条已有轨迹里的每个动作打分。我们调整两个维度。一是给它看什么：截至该动作的轨迹（<em>Prefix</em>，前缀），或者整条轨迹（<em>Hindsight</em>，事后回看）。二是问它什么：做完这个动作后任务能不能成功（<em>Value</em>），或者这个动作有没有推动目标达成（<em>Progress</em>）。",
 "<span class=\"role-t\">Teacher.</span> The model scores the actions of the policy being trained, and the scores enter GRPO as step-level credit. It stays frozen and is not used at test time.": "<span class=\"role-t\">老师（Teacher）。</span>模型给正在训练的策略做出的动作打分，分数作为步级信用信号接入 GRPO。模型参数始终冻结，测试时也不参与。",
 "<a class=\"fig-ref\" href=\"#fig-1\">Figure 1</a> plays the three roles on the paper's running example: put a heated mug on a table.": "<a class=\"fig-ref\" href=\"#fig-1\">图 1</a>沿用论文的主线例子“把加热过的杯子放到桌上”，依次演示这三种角色。",
 "<span class=\"m1-tn\">1</span>Actor<i class=\"m1-prog\"></i>": "<span class=\"m1-tn\">1</span>执行者<i class=\"m1-prog\"></i>",
 "<span class=\"m1-tn\">2</span>Judge<i class=\"m1-prog\"></i>": "<span class=\"m1-tn\">2</span>裁判<i class=\"m1-prog\"></i>",
 "<span class=\"m1-tn\">3</span>Teacher<i class=\"m1-prog\"></i>": "<span class=\"m1-tn\">3</span>老师<i class=\"m1-prog\"></i>",
 "<b>Actor</b><span>picks the next action</span>": "<b>执行者</b><span>选下一步动作</span>",
 "<b>Judge</b><span>scores a recorded action</span>": "<b>裁判</b><span>给已有轨迹里的动作打分</span>",
 "Recorded episode: put a heated mug in the cabinet": "历史回合：把加热过的杯子放进柜子",
 "<b>Teacher</b><span>scores the policy's own rollouts</span>": "<b>老师</b><span>给策略自己生成的 rollout 打分</span>",
 "Decision model": "决策模型",
 "question + context → typed answer. Here JEV, one of the six models we test.": "问题 + 上下文 → 固定格式的答案。示例模型是 JEV，本文评测的六个模型之一。",
 "Choice probabilities": "各选项概率",
 "Easier subgoal first: the task is left incomplete.": "先做了容易的子目标，任务没能完成。",
 "Same question; seeing the mug heated shows why it mattered.": "问题不变；看到后面加热了杯子，才明白这一步为什么要紧。",
 "The no-op is pushed down; taking the cold mug back is credited.": "无效动作的优势调低，取回冷杯子的那一步得到加分。",
 "<b>Figure 1.</b> One decision model, queried three ways on heated-mug tasks. <b>Actor:</b> JEV’s choice probabilities, averaged over 116 states in which the object still needs heating, cleaning or cooling. <b>Judge:</b> JEV’s score for step 9 of a recorded episode, seeing first the steps up to it and then the whole episode (paper Table 9). <b>Teacher:</b> illustrative scores from the paper’s Figure 1, centred within the group and added to GRPO’s outcome advantage. Use the tabs to jump to a role.": "<b>图 1：</b>同一个决策模型在“加热杯子”类任务上的三种问法。<b>执行者：</b>JEV 在 116 个状态上的平均选项概率，这些状态里物体都还需要加热、清洗或冷却。<b>裁判：</b>JEV 对一个历史回合第 9 步的打分，先只给它看到第 9 步为止，再给它看整个回合（论文表 9）。<b>老师：</b>分数是论文图 1 中的示意值，减去组内均值后加到 GRPO 的结果优势上。点上方的标签可以切换角色。",
 "We evaluate six models that answer questions in this form. Three are released as <strong>dedicated decision models</strong> and are queried through their own decision APIs. The other three are <strong>general LLMs</strong> asked the same questions, either by prompting for a JSON answer or by reading the first-token probabilities of the valid answer labels. Two of these general LLMs are the base models of Decider v1.2 and GPT Decisions, so each dedicated model can be compared with its own base model.": "我们评测了六个能这样回答问题的模型。三个是正式发布的<strong>专用决策模型</strong>，通过各自的决策 API 调用。另外三个是<strong>通用大模型</strong>，问它们同样的问题，答案有两种取法：在提示里要求输出 JSON，或者直接读取合法答案标签的首 token 概率。其中两个通用大模型正好是 Decider v1.2 和 GPT Decisions 的基座，所以这两个专用模型都能和自己的基座直接对比。",
 "Model": "模型",
 "Base LLM": "基座模型",
 "How the decision interface is obtained": "决策接口的实现方式",
 "Access": "访问方式",
 "undisclosed": "未公开",
 "API only": "仅 API",
 "full fine-tuning": "全参数微调",
 "open weights": "开放权重",
 "prompting (JSON answer)": "提示（输出 JSON）",
 "constrained readout (first-token probabilities)": "限定标签读概率（首 token）",
 "We use two text environments in which some requirements must be met in a fixed order. In <strong>ALFWorld</strong> <a class=\"cite\" href=\"#ref-alfworld\">[1]</a>, an agent completes household goals with commands such as <code>go to</code>, <code>take</code> and <code>heat</code>. Its <em>Clean</em>, <em>Heat</em> and <em>Cool</em> tasks have a dependency: the object's state must change before it is placed. <em>Pick2</em> also has two requirements, two objects to place, but they can be met in either order. In <strong>WebShop</strong> <a class=\"cite\" href=\"#ref-webshop\">[2]</a>, an agent searches a catalogue and must select the required options before it buys.": "实验用到两个文本环境，环境里有些要求必须按固定顺序完成。<strong>ALFWorld</strong> <a class=\"cite\" href=\"#ref-alfworld\">[1]</a> 是家务环境，智能体用 <code>go to</code>、<code>take</code>、<code>heat</code> 等命令完成目标。其中 <em>Clean</em>、<em>Heat</em>、<em>Cool</em> 三类任务存在依赖：物体要先改变状态，才能放到指定位置。<em>Pick2</em> 也有两个要求，要放两个物体，但先放哪个都行。<strong>WebShop</strong> <a class=\"cite\" href=\"#ref-webshop\">[2]</a> 是购物环境，智能体在商品目录里搜索，下单前必须选好指定的选项。",
 "<span class=\"n\">2</span>As an actor, an easier subgoal gets in the way": "<span class=\"n\">2</span>当执行者：容易的子目标会把模型带偏",
 "Finding 1": "发现 1",
 "As actors, all six models struggle when one subgoal must be completed before another: an easier subgoal draws them away from the one that has to come first.": "六个模型当执行者时，只要一个子目标必须先于另一个完成，就都容易出错：更容易的那个子目标会把它们从该先做的一步上拉走。",
 "Ordered subgoals are where acting breaks": "子目标一有先后，执行就出问题",
 "Every model succeeds far less often on tasks with a dependency than on tasks without one (<a class=\"fig-ref\" href=\"#fig-2\">Figure 2</a>). JEV completes 70.8% of <em>Pick2</em> tasks but at most 18.8% of each dependent task type. Decider v1.2, the strongest actor overall at 63.6%, completes only 18.8% of <em>Heat</em> tasks. Because <em>Pick2</em> also has two subgoals, the gap points to their <em>order</em> rather than their number as the difficulty.": "所有模型在有依赖的任务上，成功率都远低于无依赖的任务（<a class=\"fig-ref\" href=\"#fig-2\">图 2</a>）。JEV 能完成 70.8% 的 <em>Pick2</em> 任务，但在每一类依赖任务上都不超过 18.8%。整体最强的执行者 Decider v1.2（63.6%），在 <em>Heat</em> 任务上也只有 18.8%。<em>Pick2</em> 同样有两个子目标，所以难点不在子目标的数量，而在它们的<em>顺序</em>。",
 "ALFWorld, acting": "ALFWorld，当执行者",
 "Actor success rate by task type": "执行者在各类任务上的成功率",
 "All task types": "全部类型",
 "Pick2 vs dependent": "Pick2 与依赖任务",
 "<b>Figure 2.</b> Success rates (%) of the six models acting on ALFWorld, one run per task on the evaluation tasks later used for the trained policies. <i>Pick2</i> and the three dependent types both have two subgoals; only the dependent ones fix their order. Switch to “Pick2 vs dependent” to compare those directly; hover a cell for its value.": "<b>图 2：</b>六个模型在 ALFWorld 上当执行者的成功率（%）。评估任务与后文训练策略时用的相同，每个任务跑一次。<i>Pick2</i> 和三类依赖任务都有两个子目标，区别是只有依赖任务规定了顺序。切到“Pick2 与依赖任务”可以直接对比两者；鼠标悬停在格子上可查看具体数值。",
 "The failed episodes show how the order is broken. Holding the mug at the table, the actor can place it in one action, or walk to the microwave, heat it and come back. In many failures it places the unheated mug and the task can no longer be completed as intended.": "看失败的回合，就知道顺序是怎么乱掉的。执行者拿着杯子站在桌边，这时有两种走法：一步把杯子放下，或者走到微波炉把杯子加热再回来。很多失败回合里，它直接放下了没加热的杯子，任务从此没法按要求完成。",
 "Distraction, not ignorance": "不是不会，是分心",
 "We collected 116 states, from 66 tasks, in which a single action would satisfy the easier subgoal while the required one was still unmet, and queried each actor there under two goals that differ only in the easier subgoal, for example “put a heated mug on the side table” versus “heat a mug”. Everything else, including the history, observation, candidate actions and remaining budget, is identical.": "我们从 66 个任务里挑出 116 个状态。在这些状态下，一个动作就能完成容易的子目标，而必须先做的子目标还没完成。在每个状态上，我们用两个目标分别询问执行者，两者只差那个容易的子目标，例如“把加热过的杯子放到边桌上”和“加热杯子”。其余输入完全相同，包括历史、观测、候选动作和剩余步数预算。",
 "<strong>With the full goal, JEV puts 63.8% of its probability on the easier subgoal and 14.6% on the step that must come first; without it, these become 2.5% and 77.6%</strong> (<a class=\"fig-ref\" href=\"#fig-3\">Figure 3</a>, left). All six actors shift the same way. They know the required step; the easier subgoal pulls probability away from it. Reminding them of the dependency barely helps: a generic hint changes success by −2.8 to +5.2 points, and adding a worked ordering example helps some models but not all (Figure 3, right).": "<strong>目标完整时，JEV 把 63.8% 的概率给了容易的子目标，只给必须先做的那一步 14.6%；把容易的子目标从目标里去掉，两者变成 2.5% 和 77.6%</strong>（<a class=\"fig-ref\" href=\"#fig-3\">图 3</a> 左）。六个执行者的变化方向都一样。可见它们知道该先做哪一步，只是容易的子目标把概率抢走了。提醒它们注意依赖关系也几乎没用：加一句通用提示，成功率只变化 −2.8 到 +5.2 个百分点；再给一个按正确顺序完成的示例，也只对部分模型有效（图 3 右）。",
 "JEV, 116 states": "JEV，116 个状态",
 "Where the probability goes": "概率给了谁",
 "Share of JEV's probability by action type, %": "JEV 在各类动作上的概率占比（%）",
 "Full goal": "完整目标",
 "Without the easier subgoal": "去掉容易的子目标",
 "Same 116 states, continued to the end": "同样 116 个状态，继续执行到回合结束",
 "Success with an ordering example in the prompt": "提示里加入顺序示例后的成功率",
 "Original prompt → hint plus a heated-mug example, %": "原提示 → 依赖提示 + 加热杯子示例（%）",
 "<b>Figure 3.</b> <b>Left:</b> JEV's action probabilities, grouped into the step toward the subgoal that must come first, the action that completes the easier subgoal, and everything else, with and without the easier subgoal in the goal. <b>Right:</b> success when each episode continues under the original prompt versus a dependency hint plus an ordering example. GPT Luna, which changes little, is omitted because the paper does not report its values in the text.": "<b>图 3：</b><b>左：</b>JEV 的动作概率，分三组：走向必须先完成的子目标的一步、直接完成容易子目标的动作、其他动作；对比目标里有、没有容易子目标两种情况。<b>右：</b>每个回合继续执行时的成功率，对比原提示和“依赖提示 + 顺序示例”。GPT Luna 变化很小，论文正文也没有给出具体数值，图中未画。",
 "Acting correctly here requires anticipating that the easy action leaves the task unfinished <em>before</em> any consequence is visible. A judge evaluates the action after its consequences have occurred, which is where the next section starts.": "要在这里做对，执行者得在任何后果出现<em>之前</em>就想到：这个顺手的动作会让任务做不完。裁判不一样，它在后果出现之后才评价动作。下一节就讲裁判。",
 "<span class=\"n\">3</span>As a judge, the question and the context decide": "<span class=\"n\">3</span>当裁判：问什么、看什么，决定判得准不准",
 "Finding 2": "发现 2",
 "The same models can recognise contributions they overlook as actors. Seeing the whole trajectory reveals how earlier actions feed later progress, and asking whether each action helped separates those actions from ones that change nothing.": "当执行者时忽略的贡献，同样的模型当裁判时能认出来。看到完整轨迹，才看得出前面的动作怎样为后面的进展铺路；问每个动作有没有帮助，才能把这些动作和什么都没改变的动作分开。",
 "We reused the successful continuations from the 116 states and asked each judge whether the first action taken from the diagnostic state helped achieve the goal, with outcome labels masked. Seeing the whole trajectory instead of the prefix raises the mean score of these actions for all six models; for JEV it goes from 0.41 to 0.59. That raises two questions: does a full trajectory simply make every action look good, and what does the judge actually gain from it?": "我们复用从这 116 个状态出发的成功轨迹，遮住结果标签，问每个裁判：在诊断状态下执行的第一个动作，对达成目标有没有帮助。把前缀换成完整轨迹后，六个模型给这些动作的平均分都上升了，JEV 从 0.41 升到 0.59。这就引出两个问题：完整轨迹是不是只会让所有动作都显得不错？裁判从中到底多看到了什么？",
 "Ask whether the action helped, not whether the task will succeed": "问这一步有没有用，别问任务能不能成",
 "We labelled actions in 462 ALFWorld trajectories as <em>milestones</em>, which achieve a subgoal, <em>no-ops</em>, which leave the environment unchanged, and <em>other</em>. With the whole trajectory visible, the <em>Value</em> question gives the three groups almost the same score: if the episode ends in success, every action in it “leads to success”. The <em>Progress</em> question spreads them apart for every model (<a class=\"fig-ref\" href=\"#fig-4\">Figure 4</a>). For JEV, within a trajectory, Progress scores milestones 0.36 above no-ops, against 0.05 for Value, and it ranks more milestones among each trajectory's top-scored actions, by 8.0 to 16.0 points.": "我们给 462 条 ALFWorld 轨迹里的动作打上三类标签：<em>里程碑</em>（完成某个子目标）、<em>无效动作</em>（环境没有任何变化）和<em>其他</em>。能看到完整轨迹时，<em>Value</em> 问题给这三类动作的分数几乎一样：回合最后成功了，里面每个动作都算“通向成功”。换成 <em>Progress</em> 问题，六个模型都能把三类拉开（<a class=\"fig-ref\" href=\"#fig-4\">图 4</a>）。以 JEV 为例，在同一条轨迹内，Progress 给里程碑的分数比无效动作高 0.36，Value 只高 0.05；在每条轨迹得分最高的那批动作里，Progress 选中的里程碑比例也高出 8.0 到 16.0 个百分点。",
 "ALFWorld, 462 trajectories, Hindsight context": "ALFWorld，462 条轨迹，看完整轨迹（Hindsight）",
 "Mean action score by action type": "各类动作的平均得分",
 "<b>Figure 4.</b> Mean Hindsight scores for milestone, other and no-op actions under the two questions; scores are averaged within each trajectory, then across trajectories. The bracket shows the difference between the milestone and no-op means. Pick a judge to compare; Progress separates the groups for all six.": "<b>图 4：</b>两种问题下，里程碑、其他和无效动作的 Hindsight 平均得分（先在每条轨迹内平均，再在轨迹间平均）。括线标出里程碑与无效动作的均值差。可以切换裁判模型对比：六个模型上，Progress 都能把三组分开。",
 "Show the whole trajectory": "看完整条轨迹",
 "To see what the extra context buys, we held the question fixed to Progress and revealed the trajectory step by step: the prefix, then the immediate feedback after the action, then 25%, 50%, 75% and all of what follows. Over 167 trajectories, JEV's ranking of actions within a trajectory moves by 1.95 positions on average once feedback is added, and by 3.30 positions with the full trajectory. <a class=\"fig-ref\" href=\"#fig-5\">Figure 5</a> shows one of them. Drag the slider, or press play.": "为了弄清多出来的上下文起了什么作用，我们把问题固定为 Progress，把轨迹一段段展开：先只给前缀，再加上动作之后的即时反馈，然后依次加上后续部分的 25%、50%、75% 和全部。在 167 条轨迹上，加入反馈后，JEV 对轨迹内动作的排名平均变动 1.95 位；看到完整轨迹时，平均变动 3.30 位。<a class=\"fig-ref\" href=\"#fig-5\">图 5</a> 是其中一条，可以拖动滑块，也可以点播放。",
 "JEV as a judge, Progress question": "JEV 当裁判，Progress 问题",
 "“Put a heated mug in the cabinet”: scores as more of the episode becomes visible": "“把加热过的杯子放进柜子”：看到的回合越多，各步得分怎么变",
 "Visible context": "能看到的内容",
 "<b>Figure 5.</b> JEV's Progress scores for all 12 actions of one episode (paper Table 9). The mug is put in the cabinet before it is heated (step 6), taken back (7), heated in the microwave (8 to 10) and put back (12). Each bar is the score of that action when the judge sees the episode up to the action, plus the immediate feedback, plus 25%, 50%, 75% or all of the remaining steps.": "<b>图 5：</b>JEV 对同一回合全部 12 个动作的 Progress 打分（论文表 9）。这个回合里，杯子没加热就放进了柜子（第 6 步），随后取回（7），用微波炉加热（8 到 10），最后放回柜子（12）。每根柱子是裁判对该动作的打分，裁判依次能看到：到该动作为止的回合，加上即时反馈，再加上后续步骤的 25%、50%、75% 或全部。",
 "Under the prefix, JEV rates the premature placement (step 6) at 0.79 and going to the microwave (8) and opening it (9) at only 0.23 and 0.20, the same preference for the easier subgoal that the actor showed. Immediate feedback makes it worse: placement rises to 0.90. Only as the continuation comes into view do the microwave steps earn credit; opening the microwave reaches 0.66 once heating is visible and 0.76 with the full trajectory. The repeated <code>look</code> (step 2) stays low throughout, because the prefix alone already shows that it repeats step 1.": "只看前缀时，JEV 给过早放置（第 6 步）打 0.79，给走向微波炉（8）和打开微波炉（9）只打 0.23 和 0.20。这和执行者偏向容易子目标是同一个毛病。加上即时反馈反而更糟，放置升到 0.90。直到后续步骤逐渐露出来，微波炉那几步才开始得分：一看到加热，打开微波炉就升到 0.66，看到完整轨迹时是 0.76。重复的 <code>look</code>（第 2 步）始终得分很低，因为光看前缀就知道它重复了第 1 步。",
 "The two dedicated decision models whose base LLM is disclosed, Decider v1.2 and GPT Decisions, also judge more accurately than that base LLM given the same question, at 28% to 43% lower cost per score.": "Decider v1.2 和 GPT Decisions 公开了基座模型。问同样的问题，这两个专用决策模型当裁判都比各自的基座更准，每次打分的成本还低 28% 到 43%。",
 "<span class=\"n\">4</span>As a teacher, the best judge gives the best signal": "<span class=\"n\">4</span>当老师：裁判当得最好，教得也最好",
 "Finding 3": "发现 3",
 "The judgments that best separate useful from useless actions also train the strongest policies, and the gains are largest on the tasks the teacher fails as an actor.": "最能分清有用和无用动作的打分方式，训练出的策略也最强；提升最大的，恰恰是老师自己当执行者时做不成的任务。",
 "From scores to advantages": "从打分到优势",
 "GRPO gives every action in a rollout the same outcome advantage. For each task the policy samples a group of trajectories; after they finish, the teacher <span class=\"mi\">D</span> scores every executed action <span class=\"mi\">t</span> of every trajectory <span class=\"mi\">τ<sub>i</sub></span> from the goal and the trajectory alone, with no rewards, success labels or hidden state:": "GRPO 给一条 rollout 里的所有动作同一个结果优势。对每个任务，策略采样一组轨迹；轨迹跑完后，老师 <span class=\"mi\">D</span> 只看目标和轨迹本身，给每条轨迹 <span class=\"mi\">τ<sub>i</sub></span> 里执行过的每个动作 <span class=\"mi\">t</span> 打分，不用奖励和成功标签，也不看隐藏状态：",
 "The scores are centred on the mean <span class=\"mi\">s̄</span> over all scored actions in the group and added with weight λ = 0.5. They are deliberately not divided by their standard deviation, so a group in which the teacher hardly distinguishes actions receives only small adjustments. <a class=\"fig-ref\" href=\"#fig-6\">Figure 6</a> shows what the teacher term does to the two rollouts from Figure 1.": "分数先减去组内所有已打分动作的均值 <span class=\"mi\">s̄</span>，再乘以权重 λ = 0.5 加到优势上。这里故意不除以标准差：如果老师在某一组里几乎分不出动作好坏，这一组得到的调整也就很小。<a class=\"fig-ref\" href=\"#fig-6\">图 6</a> 展示了老师项对图 1 那两条 rollout 的影响。",
 "Illustrative group of two rollouts": "示意：同一组的两条 rollout",
 "What the teacher adds to each action's advantage": "老师给每个动作的优势加了多少",
 "<b>Figure 6.</b> λ(<i>s</i> − <i>s̄</i>) for each action, using the illustrative teacher scores of Figure 1 (group mean 0.71). Bars above zero receive a larger advantage than GRPO alone would give, bars below a smaller one. The outcome advantage itself is the same for every action of a rollout, so only the teacher term distinguishes them. The paper trains with λ = 0.5.": "<b>图 6：</b>每个动作的 λ(<i>s</i> − <i>s̄</i>)，老师分数取图 1 中的示意值（组均值 0.71）。柱子在零线以上，表示这个动作的优势比单用 GRPO 时大；在零线以下则更小。同一条 rollout 里所有动作的结果优势相同，能把它们区分开的只有老师项。论文训练时取 λ = 0.5。",
 "Results": "实验结果",
 "We train Qwen2.5-1.5B-Instruct with JEV as the teacher under all four combinations of question and context, and compare against GRPO with outcome rewards alone (results from GiGPO <a class=\"cite\" href=\"#ref-gigpo\">[3]</a>). Each policy is evaluated with three seeds. <strong>Hindsight + Progress gives the highest success on both environments: 72.8% → 82.9% on ALFWorld and 56.8% → 71.4% on WebShop.</strong> It improves on every ALFWorld task type, most on <em>Cool</em> (+23.0) and <em>Look</em> (+20.7). With the prefix only, the two questions perform about the same. The ordering matches the judge analysis: under Hindsight, the Value question gives every action of an episode nearly the same score and so says little about which actions helped.": "我们用 JEV 当老师训练 Qwen2.5-1.5B-Instruct，问题和上下文的四种组合都试了一遍，基线是只用结果奖励的 GRPO（结果取自 GiGPO <a class=\"cite\" href=\"#ref-gigpo\">[3]</a>）。每个策略用三个随机种子评估。<strong>Hindsight + Progress 在两个环境上都最好：ALFWorld 成功率从 72.8% 提升到 82.9%，WebShop 从 56.8% 提升到 71.4%。</strong>ALFWorld 的每一类任务都有提升，<em>Cool</em>（+23.0）和 <em>Look</em>（+20.7）最多。只看前缀时，两种问题效果相当。这个排序和前面裁判分析的结论一致：在 Hindsight 下，Value 问题给同一回合所有动作的分数都差不多，说明不了哪些动作有用。",
 "Qwen2.5-1.5B-Instruct, mean of three seeds": "Qwen2.5-1.5B-Instruct，三个种子取平均",
 "Success rate, teacher-trained policy vs GRPO": "成功率：有老师的策略与 GRPO 对比",
 "<span><i style=\"background:var(--base-2)\"></i>GRPO (outcome reward only)</span><span><i id=\"f7-key\" style=\"background:var(--tea)\"></i><span id=\"f7-name\">Hindsight + Progress</span></span><span>whiskers: ± std over seeds</span>": "<span><i style=\"background:var(--base-2)\"></i>GRPO（仅结果奖励）</span><span><i id=\"f7-key\" style=\"background:var(--tea)\"></i><span id=\"f7-name\">Hindsight + Progress</span></span><span>误差线：不同种子间的 ± 标准差</span>",
 "<b>Figure 7.</b> Success rates (%) of the 1.5B policy trained with JEV as the teacher under each question and context, against GRPO. The last two groups are overall ALFWorld success and WebShop success. Switch settings to compare; Hindsight + Progress is the best setting on both environments. The 7B option shows the same recipe on Qwen2.5-7B-Instruct.": "<b>图 7：</b>以 JEV 为老师、在不同问题与上下文设置下训练的 1.5B 策略的成功率（%），对照为 GRPO。最后两组分别是 ALFWorld 总体和 WebShop 的成功率。可以切换设置对比，Hindsight + Progress 在两个环境上都最好。选 7B 可查看同样做法在 Qwen2.5-7B-Instruct 上的结果。",
 "The gain holds at 7B, from 77.6% to 83.8% on ALFWorld and from 66.1% to 73.6% on WebShop, and <strong>the 1.5B policy taught this way outperforms the 7B policy trained with outcome rewards alone on both environments.</strong> Hindsight + Progress also finishes sooner: it completes 74.5% of ALFWorld tasks within 20 actions, against 63.6% to 69.5% for the other settings, and 71.1% of WebShop tasks within 10 actions, against 60.9% to 62.2%.": "换到 7B，提升依然在：ALFWorld 从 77.6% 到 83.8%，WebShop 从 66.1% 到 73.6%。<strong>这样教出来的 1.5B 策略，在两个环境上都胜过只用结果奖励训练的 7B 策略。</strong>Hindsight + Progress 完成任务也更快：ALFWorld 上 74.5% 的任务在 20 个动作以内完成，其他设置只有 63.6% 到 69.5%；WebShop 上 71.1% 的任务在 10 个动作以内完成，其他设置为 60.9% 到 62.2%。",
 "Learning beyond the teacher": "学生超过老师",
 "On the same ALFWorld evaluation tasks, JEV completes 42.9% as an actor; the 1.5B policy trained on its scores completes 82.9%. <strong>The largest gains are on the dependent tasks, the ones JEV handles worst as an actor</strong>: there the policy reaches 86.8%, 6.9 to 16.2 points above the other question and context settings, while JEV itself completes only 14.7% of them (<a class=\"fig-ref\" href=\"#fig-8\">Figure 8</a>). The teacher does not need to solve a task to provide a useful signal for it.": "在同一批 ALFWorld 评估任务上，JEV 亲自执行只完成 42.9%，用它的打分训练出的 1.5B 策略完成 82.9%。<strong>提升最大的，正是 JEV 当执行者时最不擅长的依赖任务</strong>：策略在这类任务上达到 86.8%，比其他问题与上下文设置高 6.9 到 16.2 个百分点，而 JEV 自己只能完成其中的 14.7%（<a class=\"fig-ref\" href=\"#fig-8\">图 8</a>）。老师自己做不成的任务，照样能给出有用的训练信号。",
 "ALFWorld, same evaluation tasks": "ALFWorld，同一批评估任务",
 "JEV acting vs the 1.5B policy JEV taught": "JEV 亲自执行，对比它教出的 1.5B 策略",
 "<span><i style=\"background:var(--act)\"></i>JEV as actor</span><span><i style=\"background:var(--tea)\"></i>1.5B policy trained with JEV (Hindsight + Progress)</span>": "<span><i style=\"background:var(--act)\"></i>JEV 当执行者</span><span><i style=\"background:var(--tea)\"></i>JEV 教出的 1.5B 策略（Hindsight + Progress）</span>",
 "<b>Figure 8.</b> Success rates (%) by task type. The arrow runs from JEV acting on its own (Table 2) to the policy it taught (Table 3). The policy surpasses its teacher everywhere except <i>Pick2</i>, and by the widest margins on the three dependent types.": "<b>图 8：</b>各类任务的成功率（%）。箭头从 JEV 亲自执行的结果（表 2）指向它教出的策略（表 3）。除 <i>Pick2</i> 外，学生在所有类型上都超过了老师，三类依赖任务上差距最大。",
 "<strong>Cost.</strong> We query JEV through OpenRouter at 0.042 USD per million input tokens to score every executed action during training: 150 steps, 16 tasks per batch, 8 rollouts per task. Scoring an entire training run costs between 22.21 and 30.07 USD.": "<strong>成本。</strong>训练中每个执行过的动作都要打分。我们通过 OpenRouter 调用 JEV，输入价格为每百万 token 0.042 美元；训练共 150 步，每批 16 个任务，每个任务 8 条 rollout。一次完整训练的打分费用在 22.21 到 30.07 美元之间。",
 "Hindsight + Progress run": "Hindsight + Progress 训练",
 "Max actions per rollout": "每条 rollout 最多动作数",
 "Teacher API cost (USD)": "老师 API 费用（美元）",
 "<span class=\"n\">5</span>Takeaways for using decision models in agents": "<span class=\"n\">5</span>给智能体用决策模型的几点启示",
 "<strong>Actors know the required step but are drawn to the easier one.</strong> They choose the right step when it is the only subgoal, and general reminders do not stop the error. When a decision model must act, restructuring the goal into ordered subgoals is more promising than adding instructions.": "<strong>执行者知道该做哪一步，只是注意力被容易的那一步吸走了。</strong>当必须先做的那一步是唯一的子目标时，它们能选对；泛泛的提醒纠正不了这个错误。如果非得让决策模型去执行，把目标拆成有先后的子目标，比多加指令更有希望。",
 "<strong>The question sets the granularity of the signal.</strong> Asking about the eventual outcome gives every action of a trajectory a similar score and largely repeats the outcome reward; asking about each action's contribution separates them.": "<strong>问题决定信号的粒度。</strong>问最终结果，轨迹里每个动作的分数都差不多，基本是把结果奖励再说一遍；问每个动作的贡献，才能把它们分开。",
 "<strong>Hindsight targets the actor's own failure.</strong> Seeing the whole trajectory lets a judge credit the steps toward the subgoal that must come first. Decision models are best used to score actions after an episode, as in RL training, and are less suited to filtering actions online, where only the prefix exists.": "<strong>Hindsight 针对的正是执行者犯错的地方。</strong>看到完整轨迹，裁判才能给走向必须先完成的子目标的那些步骤记功。所以决策模型最适合在回合结束后给动作打分，比如 RL 训练；不太适合在线筛选动作，因为那时手里只有前缀。",
 "<strong>Screen judges before training.</strong> Judging recorded trajectories identified the question and context that trained the best policy, at a small fraction of the cost of an RL run. Choose a teacher by how well it judges, not by how well it acts.": "<strong>训练前先挑裁判。</strong>只在已有轨迹上比较评判效果，我们就找到了能训练出最佳策略的问题和上下文，花费只占一次 RL 训练的一小部分。选老师，要看它判得准不准，而不是自己做得好不好。",
 "<strong>Step-level supervision becomes affordable.</strong> A frozen decision model, queried after each episode and absent at test time, costs tens of dollars per run and lets a small policy outperform a larger one trained on outcomes alone.": "<strong>步级监督不再昂贵。</strong>决策模型参数冻结，只在每个回合结束后调用，测试时用不到。每次训练花几十美元，就能让小策略超过只用结果奖励训练的大策略。",
 "The full list of references, the prompts and the appendix experiments are in the <a class=\"tx\" href=\"https://arxiv.org/abs/2611.17167\" rel=\"noopener\" target=\"_blank\">paper</a>.": "完整参考文献、提示词和附录实验见<a class=\"tx\" href=\"https://arxiv.org/abs/2611.17167\" rel=\"noopener\" target=\"_blank\">论文</a>。",
 "Three robots in a watercolour landscape: an amber actor weighing which path to take, a blue judge inspecting footsteps with a magnifying glass, and a green teacher pointing at a board for a smaller student robot": "水彩风景里有三个机器人：琥珀色的执行者在两条路之间犹豫，蓝色的裁判拿着放大镜查看脚印，绿色的老师指着黑板给一个小机器人讲课",
 "Role": "角色",
 "Show": "显示",
 "Goal": "目标",
 "Judge": "裁判",
 "s sub i t equals D of g, tau i, t, between 0 and 1; A sub i t equals A out plus lambda times s sub i t minus s bar": "s 下标 i t 等于 D 作用于 g、τ i、t，取值在 0 到 1 之间；A 下标 i t 等于 A out 加上 λ 乘以 s 下标 i t 减去 s 均值",
 "Teacher setting": "老师设置",
